#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:389
msgid "**2) Find the fluid velocity at the center of the floc:**"
msgstr "**2) Encontrar la velocidad del fluido en el centro del flóculo:**"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:391
msgid ""
"Now, we want to determine the velocity at the center of the floc. For flow "
"between parallel plates we determined that,"
msgstr ""
"Ahora, queremos determinar la velocidad en el centro del flóculo. Para el "
"flujo entre placas paralelas determinamos que,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:393
msgid ""
"\\frac{d v_{\\alpha_{Plate}}}{dy}_{y = 0} = \\frac{6 \\bar "
"v_{\\alpha_{Plate}}}{S}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:397
msgid ""
"The center of the floc is approximately half of the floc diameter, "
":math:`D_{floc}`. So, to find the fluid velocity at the center of the floc, "
"we linearize the differential and plug in :math:`\\frac{D_{floc}}{2}` to "
"yield,"
msgstr ""
"El centro del flóculo es aproximadamente la mitad del diámetro del fló"
"culo, :math:`D_{floc}`. Así que, para encontrar la velocidad del fluid"
"o en el centro del flóculo, linealizamos el diferencial y conectamos :"
"math:`\\frac{D_{floc}}{2}` para obtener,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:399
msgid ""
"v_{\\alpha} \\approx \\frac{6 \\bar v_{\\alpha_{Plate}}}{S} "
"\\frac{D_{floc}}{2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:403
msgid ""
"Substituting by the trigonometric relationship :math:`\\bar "
"v_{\\alpha_{Plate}} = (\\frac{\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{sin\\alpha})`, we find "
"the fluid velocity at the center of the floc as,"
msgstr ""
"Sustituyendo por la relación trigonométrica :math:`\\bar v_{\\alpha_{Plate}}"
" = (\\frac{\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{sin\\alpha})`, encontramos la velocidad del "
"fluido en el centro del flóculo como,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:405
msgid ""
"\\bar v_{\\alpha_{Plate}} \\approx \\frac{3 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}} "
"D_{floc}}{Ssin\\alpha}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:416
msgid "Fluid velocity at the center of the floc."
msgstr "Velocidad del fluido en el centro del flóculo."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:418
msgid ""
"**3) Find terminal velocity of the floc down the plate (for the case of zero"
" velocity fluid):**"
msgstr ""
"**3) Encontrar la velocidad terminal del flóculo a lo largo de la placa (en "
"el caso de fluido de velocidad cero):**"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:421
msgid "The terminal velocity of a floc is given by Equation :eq:`vt_of_floc`."
msgstr ""
"La velocidad terminal de un flóculo está dada por la ecuación "
":eq:`vt_of_floc`."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:430
msgid ""
"Terminal velocity of the floc down the plate (for the case of zero velocity "
"fluid)."
msgstr ""
"Velocidad terminal del flóculo a lo largo de la placa (en el caso de fluido "
"de velocidad cero)."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:430
msgid "Terminal velocity of the floc down the plate."
msgstr "Velocidad terminal del flóculo a lo largo de la placa."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:432
msgid ""
"**4) Set the fluid velocity at the center of the floc equal to the terminal "
"velocity of the floc to find the critical case of no movement, and the "
"required plate spacing:**"
msgstr ""
"**4) Ajustar la velocidad del fluido en el centro del flóculo igual a la "
"velocidad terminal del flóculo para encontrar el caso crítico de ausencia de"
" movimiento y el espaciado de placas requerido:**"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:434
msgid ""
"The floc settles due to gravitational forces. First, the :math:`\\alpha` "
"component of the gravitational settling force, :math:`v_{t,\\alpha}`, must "
"be found by trigonometric relationships."
msgstr ""
"El flóculo se asienta debido a fuerzas gravitatorias. Primero, el componente"
" :math:`\\alpha` de la fuerza de sedimentación gravitatoria, "
":math:`v_{t,\\alpha}`, debe encontrarse mediante relaciones trigonométricas."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:436
msgid "v_{t,\\alpha} = v_t sin\\alpha"
msgstr "v_{t,\\alpha} = v_t sin\\alpha"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:440
msgid "Setting :math:`v_{\\alpha} = v_{t,\\alpha}` yields,"
msgstr "Al establecer :math:`v_{\\alpha} = v_{t,\\alpha}` se da como resultado,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:442
msgid "\\frac{3 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}} D_{floc}}{Ssin\\alpha} \\approx v_t sin\\alpha"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:446
msgid "Solving for :math:`S` to determine plate spacing,"
msgstr "Resolviendo para :math:`S` determinar el espaciado de placas,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:448
msgid "S \\approx \\frac{3 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}} D_{floc}}{v_t sin^2\\alpha}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:452
msgid ""
"In this equation, we have both :math:`v_t` and :math:`D_{floc}`, but we can "
"simplify further because we know that :math:`v_t` and :math:`D_{floc}` are "
"related by the relationship shown in step 3. The goal is to ensure that "
"flocs that settle to the plates do not roll up. We replace the unknown "
"diameter of the floc with its terminal velocity and set that to be the "
"capture velocity, :math:`v_c` for the plate settler."
msgstr ""
"En esta ecuación, tenemos tanto :math:`v_t` como :math:`D_{floc}`, per"
"o podemos simplificar aún más porque sabemos que :math:`v_t` y :math:`"
"D_{floc}` están relacionados por la relación mostrada en el paso 3. El"
" objetivo es asegurar que los flóculos que se sedimentan en las placas"
" no sean arrastrados hacia arriba. Reemplazamos el diámetro desconocid"
"o del flóculo por su velocidad terminal y fijamos que sea la velocidad"
" de captura, :math:`v_c` para la placa sedimentadora."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:454
msgid ""
"S_{min} \\approx \\frac{3 D_{cp}}{sin^2\\alpha} \\frac{\\bar "
"v_{z_{Plate}}}{v_c}  \\left( \\frac{18 v_c \\nu }{D_{cp}^2g} \\frac{ "
"\\rho_{H_2O}}{ \\rho_{cp} - \\rho_{H_2O}} \\right) ^{\\frac{1}{ "
"\\Pi_{fractal} - 1}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:459
msgid ""
":math:`S_{min}` is the smallest spacing that will allow a floc with a given "
"settling velocity to remain stationary on the slope and not be carried "
"upward by rollup."
msgstr ""
":math:`S_{min}` es el espaciamiento más pequeño que permitirá que un flóculo"
" con una velocidad de sedimentación determinada permanezca estacionario en "
"la pendiente y no sea llevado hacia arriba por el rollup."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:461
msgid ""
"If the fractal dimension, :math:`\\Pi_{fractal}` has a value of 2, then "
"Equation :eq:`Plate_S_min_of_fractal` can be simplified."
msgstr ""
"Si la dimensión fractal, :math:`\\Pi_{fractal}` tiene un valor de 2, "
"entonces la ecuación :eq:`Plate_S_min_of_fractal` puede simplificarse."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:463
msgid ""
"S_{min} \\approx \\frac{3 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{\\sin^2 \\alpha} \\left( "
"\\frac{18 \\nu}{g D_{cp}} \\frac{\\rho_{H_2O}}{\\rho_{cp} - \\rho_{H_2O}} "
"\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:468
msgid ""
"A plot of Equation :eq:`Plate_S_min_of_fractal_of_2` reveals that the "
"minimum spacing is strongly influenced by the density of the core particle "
"and by the temperature. The minimum spacing increases as the size of the "
"primary particle, :math:`D_{cp}`, decreases. This is an important insight "
"because flocs that are made of coagulant nanoparticles and dissolved "
"organics are the most difficult flocs to capture. Flocs made of coagulant "
"nanoparticles are less dense than flocs made of clay. Coagulant nanoparticle"
" flocs are produced when water treatment plants are used to remove dissolved"
" organics or arsenic or when high coagulant dosages are used."
msgstr ""
"Un gráfico de la Ecuación :eq:`Plate_S_min_of_fractal_of_2` revela que"
" el espaciamiento mínimo está fuertemente influenciado por la densidad"
" de la partícula central y por la temperatura. El espaciamiento mínimo"
" aumenta a medida que disminuye el tamaño de la partícula primaria, :m"
"ath:`D_{cp}`,. Esto es una información importante porque los flóculos "
"formados por nanopartículas coagulantes y orgánicos disueltos son los "
"flóculos más difíciles de capturar. Los flóculos hechos de nanopartícu"
"las coagulantes son menos densos que los flóculos hechos de arcilla. L"
"os flóculos de nanopartículas coagulantes se producen cuando se utiliz"
"an plantas de tratamiento de agua para eliminar orgánicos disueltos o "
"arsénico o cuando se emplean dosis elevadas de coagulante."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:477
msgid "Floc roll up as a function of core particle density and temperatures"
msgstr ""
"Arrastre ascendente de flóculos en función de la densidad de las partí"
"culas primarias y la temperatura"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:477
msgid "Plate settler spacing must increase to capture low density flocs."
msgstr ""
"placa sedimentadora espacio debe aumentar para capturar flóculos de baja "
"densidad."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:479
msgid ""
"Given that AguaClara uses a lower upflow velocity, :math:`\\bar "
"v_{z_{Plate}}`, than many plate settler designs it is reasonable for us to "
"use more closely spaced plates. More work is required to characterize the "
"density and size of the core particles as a function of raw water "
"constituents to provide guidance on the required plate spacing."
msgstr ""
"Dado que AguaClara utiliza una velocidad de flujo ascendente menor, :m"
"ath:`\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}`, que muchos diseños placa sedimentadora, es r"
"azonable que utilicemos placas más próximas entre sí. Se requiere más "
"trabajo para caracterizar la densidad y el tamaño de las partículas de"
"l núcleo en función de agua cruda constituyentes para guiar el espacia"
"do de placas requerido."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:481
msgid ""
"AguaClara plate settlers are currently using separations of 2.5 cm, which is"
" far above the constraint of floc roll up except for very low density flocs."
" As floc density decreases, as we expect for organic matter, minimum spacing"
" increases. However, we don't yet know what that spacing is or where the "
"boundary is because we don't know the properties of the humic acid-coagulant"
" flocs. Further research is required here to determine the floc properties "
"of flocs that are dominated by dissolved organic matter."
msgstr ""
"Las placas sedimentadoras de AguaClara utilizan actualmente un espacia"
"miento de 2,5 cm, muy superior al mínimo impuesto por la restricción d"
"e arrastre ascendente, excepto para flóculos de muy baja densidad. A m"
"edida que disminuye la densidad de los flóculos, como cabe esperar cua"
"ndo contienen materia orgánica, aumenta el espaciamiento mínimo. Sin e"
"mbargo, aún no conocemos ese espaciamiento ni el límite porque descono"
"cemos las propiedades de los flóculos formados por ácido húmico y coag"
"ulante. Se requiere más investigación para determinar las propiedades "
"de los flóculos dominados por materia orgánica disuelta."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:486
msgid "Head Loss Through Plate Settlers"
msgstr "Pérdida de carga a través de las placas sedimentadoras"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:488
msgid ""
"Flow through the clarifier is controlled by head loss in an attempt to "
"achieve flow uniformity. We have already explained that :ref:`plate settler "
"spacing impacts head loss "
"<heading_Clarifier_Plate_Settlers_Head_Loss_Intro>`, but by what "
"mathematical relationship? Will putting plate settlers closer together "
"result in more or less head loss? This question is complicated because "
"closer plate settlers would create more shear and head loss, but shorter "
"plate settlers have less area which would decrease the head loss."
msgstr ""
"El flujo a través del clarificador es controlado por pérdida de carga "
"en un intento de lograr uniformidad del flujo. Ya hemos explicado que "
":ref:`plate settler spacing impacts head loss <heading_Clarifier_Plate"
"_Settlers_Head_Loss_Intro>`, pero ¿por qué relación matemática? ¿Acerc"
"ando las placas sedimentadoras resultará en más o menos pérdida de car"
"ga? Esta cuestión es complicada porque las placas sedimentadoras más c"
"ercanas crearían más cizallamiento y pérdida de carga, pero las placas"
" sedimentadoras más cortos tienen menos área, lo que disminuiría la pé"
"rdida de carga."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:490
msgid ""
"Let's start with a force balance similar to the derivation for head loss "
"between parallel plates as done previously for Equation "
":eq:`parallel_plate_laminar_headloss`. Assume that there is a fully "
"established velocity profile that is parabolic with laminar flow. The forces"
" that we care about are shear forces on the walls of the plate settlers and "
"the differential pressure from flow in the direction of the velocity."
msgstr ""
"Empecemos con un balance de fuerzas similar a la derivación para pérdi"
"da de carga entre placas paralelas, como se hizo previamente para la E"
"cuación :eq:`parallel_plate_laminar_headloss`. Supongamos que existe u"
"n perfil de velocidad completamente establecido que es parabólico con "
"flujo laminar. Las fuerzas que nos importan son las fuerzas de corte e"
"n las paredes de las placas sedimentadoras y la presión diferencial de"
"l flujo en la dirección de la velocidad."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:499
msgid "Velocity, shear forces, and pressure loss through plate settlers."
msgstr ""
"Velocidad, fuerzas de corte y pérdida de presión a través de las placa"
"s sedimentadoras."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:501
msgid ""
"The shear forces act over the area of the two plates, resulting in "
":math:`F_{shear} = 2 \\tau L W` where :math:`\\tau` is the viscous shear "
"component."
msgstr ""
"Las fuerzas de corte actúan sobre el área de las dos placas, resultando en "
":math:`F_{shear} = 2 \\tau L W` donde :math:`\\tau` es el componente viscoso"
" de cizalladura."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:503
msgid ""
"The pressure force is exerted over the entire width of the plate and the "
"plate spacing. Pressure at the entrance of the plate settlers is different "
"from the exit of the plate settlers by :math:`\\Delta P`. The resulting "
"pressure force is :math:`F_{pressure} = \\Delta P W S`. So,"
msgstr ""
"La fuerza de presión se ejerce sobre todo el ancho de la placa y el es"
"paciamiento de la placa. La presión en la entrada de las placas sedime"
"ntadoras es diferente de la salida de las placas sedimentadoras por :m"
"ath:`\\Delta P`. La fuerza de presión resultante es :math:`F_{pressure}"
" = \\Delta P W S`. Así,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:505
msgid "F_{shear} = F_{pressure}"
msgstr "F_{shear} = F_{pressure}"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:509
msgid "2 \\tau L W = \\Delta P W S"
msgstr "2 \\tau L W = \\delta P W S"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:513
msgid ""
"Dividing both sides by width, :math:`W`, and solving for :math:`\\Delta P` "
"yields,"
msgstr ""
"Dividiendo ambos lados por ancho, :math:`W`, y resolviendo para "
":math:`\\Delta P` se obtiene,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:515
msgid "\\Delta P = \\frac{2 \\tau L}{S}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:519
msgid ""
"We need to figure out what each of the terms on the right side of the "
"equation is equal to so we can calculate :math:`\\Delta P`. Ultimlately, we "
"need :math:`\\Delta P` to calculate head loss because :math:`h_L = "
"\\frac{\\Delta P}{\\rho g}`."
msgstr ""
"Necesitamos averiguar a qué equivale cada uno de los términos en el lado "
"derecho de la ecuación para poder calcular :math:`\\Delta P`. Últimamente, "
"necesitamos :math:`\\Delta P` para calcular pérdida de carga porque "
":math:`h_L = \\frac{\\Delta P}{\\rho g}`."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:521
msgid ""
":math:`\\tau =\\mu \\frac{du}{dy}`, where :math:`\\tau` is shear, "
":math:`\\mu` is the viscosity, and :math:`\\frac{du}{dy}` is the velocity "
"gradient. Using the Navier-Stokes equation, we can find the velocity "
"gradient as a function of the average velocity between the plates, yielding "
"shear based on the vertical velocity entering the plates as,"
msgstr ""
":math:`\\tau =\\mu \\frac{du}{dy}`, donde :math:`\\tau` es cizallamiento, "
":math:`\\mu` es la viscosidad y :math:`\\frac{du}{dy}` es el gradiente de "
"velocidad. Usando la ecuación de Navier-Stokes, podemos encontrar el "
"gradiente de velocidad en función de la velocidad media entre las placas, "
"dando lugar a un corte basado en la velocidad vertical que entra en las "
"placas como,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:523
msgid "\\tau = \\mu \\frac{6 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{S sin\\alpha}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:527
msgid ""
":math:`L` is found using the equation for capture velocity, :math:`\\bar v_c"
" = \\frac{S*\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{Lsin\\alpha cos\\alpha + S}`. Capture "
"velocity is kept constant so we solve for :math:`L`,"
msgstr ""
":math:`L` se encuentra usando la ecuación para la velocidad de captura, "
":math:`\\bar v_c = \\frac{S*\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{Lsin\\alpha cos\\alpha + "
"S}`. La velocidad de captura se mantiene constante, así que resolvemos para "
":math:`L`,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:529
msgid ""
"L = \\frac{S \\left( \\frac{\\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{\\bar v_c} -1 "
"\\right)}{sin\\alpha cos\\alpha}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:533
msgid ""
"Substituting :math:`\\tau` and :math:`L` into the equation for "
":math:`\\Delta P`,"
msgstr "Sustituyendo :math:`\\tau` y :math:`L` en la ecuación para :math:`\\Delta P`,"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:535
msgid ""
"\\Delta P = 2\\mu \\left( \\frac{6 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{S sin^2 \\alpha "
"cos\\alpha} \\right) \\left( \\frac{ \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{\\bar v_c} -1 "
"\\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:539
msgid ""
"Now that we have an equation for :math:`\\Delta P`, we can solve for head "
"loss."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que tenemos una ecuación para :math:`\\Delta P`, podemos resolver para"
" pérdida de carga."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:541
msgid "h_L = \\frac{\\Delta P}{\\rho g}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:545
msgid ""
"h_L = 2 \\frac{\\mu}{\\rho g} \\left( \\frac{6 \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{S sin^2 "
"\\alpha cos\\alpha} \\right) \\left( \\frac{ \\bar v_{z_{Plate}}}{\\bar v_c}"
" -1 \\right)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:550
msgid ""
"Recall that head loss through plate settlers is really small, on the order "
"of micrometers, :math:`\\mu m`. We are interested in understanding how the "
"head loss relates to velocity, through the relation :math:`v = \\sqrt{2gh}`."
" The resulting two plots show how head loss and velocity relate to plate "
"settlers (see :numref:`figure_plate_settler_headloss_spacing`)."
msgstr ""
"Recordemos que las placas sedimentadoras pérdida de carga a través son"
" realmente pequeños, del orden de micrómetros, :math:`\\mu m`. Nos inte"
"resa entender cómo se relaciona la pérdida de carga con la velocidad, "
"a través de la relación :math:`v = \\sqrt{2gh}`. Los dos gráficos resul"
"tantes muestran cómo pérdida de carga y velocidad se relacionan con la"
"s placas sedimentadoras (véase :numref:`figure_plate_settler_headloss_"
"spacing`)."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:556
msgid "Jet Velocity"
msgstr "Velocidad del chorro"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:558
msgid ""
":math:`\\bar v_{jet}` is defined as the velocity of the water jet exiting "
"the diffuser. After exiting the diffuser, this water jet is sent into the "
"jet reverser to make a 180 degree turn. Does the water jet change pressure "
"or velocity as it exits the jet reverser? Do we need to consider the effects"
" of a *vena contracta*?"
msgstr ""
":math:`\\bar v_{jet}` se define como la velocidad del chorro de agua que "
"sale del difusor. Después de salir del difusor, este chorro de agua se envía"
" al inversor del chorro para realizar un giro de 180 grados. ¿El chorro de "
"agua cambia de presión o velocidad al salir del inversor del chorro? "
"¿Necesitamos considerar los efectos de una *vena contracta*?"

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:560
msgid ""
"Recall that a :ref:`*vena contracta* <heading_what_is_a_vena_contracta>` is "
"associated with a change in pressure that causes a contraction and "
"subsequent acceleration of the fluid. Water exiting the diffuser is pointed "
"directly down and the streamlines are straight and parallel, which means "
"that the pressure across the streamlines is constant. Water exiting the jet "
"reverser is pointed directly up and the streamlines are straight and "
"parallel, which again means that the pressure across the streamlines is "
"constant. Because the pressure is constant at the exit of the diffuser and "
"at the exit of the jet reverser, we assume that the pressure of the water in"
" the space between those two points is also constant because there is no "
"physical barrier. If the pressure in this bottom section of the clarifier is"
" constant from the exit of the diffuser to the exit of the jet reverser, we "
"can infer that they are equal."
msgstr ""
"Recuerda que un :ref:`*vena contracta* <heading_what_is_a_vena_contracta>` "
"está asociado a un cambio de presión que provoca una contracción y posterior"
" aceleración del fluido. El agua que sale del difusor apunta directamente "
"hacia abajo y las líneas de corriente son rectas y paralelas, lo que "
"significa que la presión a través de las líneas de corriente es constante. "
"El agua que sale del inversor del chorro apunta directamente hacia arriba y "
"las líneas de corriente son rectas y paralelas, lo que de nuevo significa "
"que la presión a través de las líneas de corriente es constante. Como la "
"presión es constante en la salida del difusor y en la salida del inversor "
"del chorro, asumimos que la presión del agua en el espacio entre esos dos "
"puntos también es constante porque no hay barrera física. Si la presión en "
"esta sección inferior del clarificador es constante desde la salida del "
"difusor hasta la salida del inversor del chorro, podemos inferir que son "
"iguales."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:562
msgid ""
"By Bernoulli, if the pressures between the exit of the diffuser to the exit "
"of the jet reverser are equal then the velocities must also be equal. "
"Bernoulli is applicable here because there is no flow expansion yet. The "
"shear along the wall of the jet reverser is insignificant due to the short "
"flow path. The water accelerates to account for the directional change but "
"the absolute velocity does not change as it goes around the jet reverser."
msgstr ""
"Por Bernoulli, si las presiones entre la salida del difusor y la salida del "
"inversor del chorro son iguales, entonces las velocidades también deben ser "
"iguales. Bernoulli es aplicable aquí porque aún no hay expansión del flujo. "
"La cizalladura a lo largo de la pared del inversor del chorro es "
"insignificante debido al corto camino del flujo. El agua acelera para tener "
"en cuenta el cambio de dirección, pero la velocidad absoluta no cambia al "
"rodear el inversor del chorro."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:571
msgid "Diagram of diffuser exit and jet."
msgstr "Diagrama de la salida del difusor y el chorro."

#: ../../Clarification/Clarifier_Derivations.rst:573
msgid ""
"Therefore, the velocity at the exit of the diffuser is equal to the velocity"
" at the exit of the jet reverser."
msgstr ""
"Por lo tanto, la velocidad en la salida del difusor es igual a la velocidad "
"en la salida del inversor del chorro."

